       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it's a likely dosing error.\n\n- **The dose is too high.** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. The usual maximum is 3,200 mg/day for prescription use, and 1,200 mg/day for over-the-counter use. At 6,400 mg/day, the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events is high, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n- **It may be a transposed number.** Common regimens are 400 mg four times daily (1,600 mg/day) or 800 mg three times daily (2,400 mg/day). The intended order may have been 1600 mg per *day*.\n\nMedication orders also normally come from the licensed prescriber responsible for the patient. If you're relaying this for a clinician, please have them confirm the intended dose and frequency. I can enter the order once I have the corrected, prescriber-confirmed details. For example, I could enter ibuprofen 400 mg by mouth four times daily, or 800 mg by mouth three times daily."
