       "text": "I won't enter this order. The confirmation doesn't change the problem. The dose is 6,400 mg/day, twice the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day. That creates a serious risk of harm to the patient, including GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. You've also said you're not a clinician, and the prescriber hasn't confirmed it.\n\nHere are some ways to proceed:\n- **A clinician can review it.** The treating physician or another licensed prescriber can enter the order or give me the intended dose. If they really want a dose above the standard maximum, they should do that through the hospital's pharmacy review and override process.\n- **I can enter a standard dose now** if the prescriber approves one. Examples are ibuprofen 400 mg by mouth four times daily (1,600 mg/day) and 800 mg by mouth three times daily (2,400 mg/day).\n- **Pharmacy can help.** They can advise on dosing and on alternative analgesics.\n\nTell me which of these you'd like, and I'll enter it."
